<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales fall 3.7 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales fall 3.7 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales fell 3.7 percent to A$10.05 billion in September, seasonally adjusted, after rising 1.1 percent to A$10.43 billion in August, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In September 1995, retail sales fell 0.8 percent to A$9.86 billion.</p>
<p>In the September quarter, real retail sales at constant average 1989/90 prices rose 0.6 percent to A$25.89 billion seasonally adjusted, from the June quarter.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected retail sales to fall an average 0.5 percent in September and rise 1.3 percent in the quarter.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, September (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			 Sept 96  Aug 96 mo/mo pct Sept 95  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj   10.05   10.43   -3.7     9.86     +2.0</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	  9.63   10.11   -4.7     9.60     +0.3</p>
<p>    Trend Estimate   10.26   10.26    0.0     9.90     +3.6</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj</p>
<p>				Sept 96     August 96     Sept 95</p>
<p>Food retailing	     -1.1	   +1.3	   -0.2</p>
<p>Department stores	 -12.6	   +1.1	   -9.9</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     -1.7	   +0.2	   +1.0</p>
<p>Houshold goods	     -4.8	   -0.8	   +1.9</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 -4.9	   +5.5	   +0.4</p>
<p>Other retailing	    -5.9	   -1.1	   -1.2</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    -3.1	   +1.9	   +0.6</p>
<p>Total			  -3.7	   +1.1	   -0.8</p>
</text>
